                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>As Ed Pope points out: This is 2a very common name, 74 entries in London Trades 1811 (only one
                            from book trades, Edw. Atkinson, printer, 2 Greystock-pl, Fetter-la /
                            one schoolmaster Geo. Atkinson, academy, 105 Fenchurch-st) and 37
                            entries in the Court directory. Just possibly Joseph Atkinson DNB
                            1743-1818 playwright Godwin may have met in Ireland in 1800 (see my
                            entry for Atkinson, Capt.). Or William Atkinson DNB 1774/5-1839
                            architect or John Augustus Atkinson DNB 1774x6-1830 painter and
                            engraver</p>
